      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be honest, for me it sounds like a duplication of https://zuul-ci.org/docs/zuul/latest/config/project.html#attr-project.branches that really already gave precise control over branch-specific behavior (i.e. when adding a project to a pipeline under specific branches condition one may for example set some job variables, which is not possible on the pipeline level).\n\nHowever, I see similar already exists for GitHub and Gerrit, so I am not really against it (more configuration options, matching with other drivers, are welcome, e.g. for users relying on multiple backends):\n- https://zuul-ci.org/docs/zuul/latest/drivers/github.html#attr-pipeline.trigger.%3Cgithub%20source%3E.branch\n- https://zuul-ci.org/docs/zuul/latest/drivers/gerrit.html#attr-pipeline.trigger.%3Cgerrit%20source%3E.branch",
      "revId": "7c89a50012e0a44d2952f288eabf9501c3dabae8",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
